# NB: `CLAUDE*` and `.claude/` are deliberate — this project's Claude context is kept
# machine-local (decision 2026-07-26). It therefore reaches no collaborator, no other
# machine, and no remote/web Claude Code session. See main/.claude/_archive/README.md
# for what that costs and the one-step way to reverse it.

# NB: do NOT add a blanket `*cache*` rule here. It silently untracked 23 files
# (2.3 MB), 18 of them the `cache_*.csv` in figures_for_paper/*/source_data/ that
# README.md designates as shipped paper source data, plus the panels_cache_*.npz
# that semantic_regression_panels.py reads to render its figures. Because those
# caches determine the rendered output but were invisible to git, they drifted
# out of sync with the committed figures without anything showing up in
# `git status`. The two caches that genuinely should be ignored -- __pycache__/
# and .vector_cache -- are already listed explicitly above.
